{"status":"ok","message-type":"work","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,12]],"date-time":"2026-09-12T03:44:58Z","timestamp":1789184698931,"version":"build-2803163510"},"reference-count":75,"publisher":"American Meteorological Society","issue":"12","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2024,12,1]],"date-time":"2024-12-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1733011200000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"http:\/\/www.ametsoc.org\/PUBSReuseLicenses"}],"funder":[{"DOI":"10.13039\/100010661","name":"Horizon 2020 Framework Programme","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","award":["869550"],"award-info":[{"award-number":["869550"]}],"id":[{"id":"10.13039\/100010661","id-type":"DOI","asserted-by":"crossref"}]}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"short-container-title":[],"published-print":{"date-parts":[[2024,12]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n<jats:p>Seasonal rainfall is critical to lives and livelihoods within the Horn of Africa drylands (HAD), but it is highly variable in space and time. The main HAD rainfall seasons are typically defined as March\u2013May (MAM) and October\u2013December (OND). However, these 3-month periods are only generalized definitions of seasonality across the HAD, and local experience of rainfall may depart from these substantially. Here, we use daily rain gauge data with a duration of at least 10 years from 69 stations across the drylands of Kenya, Somalia, and Ethiopia to locally delineate key rainfall seasons. By calculating local seasonal rainfall timings, totals, and extremes, we obtain more accurate estimates of the spatial variability in rainfall delivery across the HAD, as well as climatological patterns. Results show high spatial variability in season onset, cessation, and length across the region, indicating that a homogenous classification of rainfall seasons across the HAD (e.g., MAM and OND) is inadequate for representing local rainfall characteristics. Our results show that the \u201clong rains\u201d season is not significantly longer than the \u201cshort rains\u201d season over the period of study. This could be related to the previously documented decline of the \u201clong rains\u201d seasonal totals over recent decades. Several rainfall metrics also vary spatially between seasons, and the rainfall on the most extreme days can accumulate to double the local mean seasonal total. The locally defined rainfall seasons better capture the bulk of the rainfall during the season, giving improved characterization of rainfall metrics, consistent with the aim of a better understanding of rainfall impacts on local communities.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1175\/jhm-d-23-0228.1","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2024,10,14]],"date-time":"2024-10-14T07:33:36Z","timestamp":1728891216000},"page":"1845-1861","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":2,"title":["Locally Defined Seasonal Rainfall Characteristics within the Horn of Africa Drylands from Rain Gauge Observations"],"prefix":"10.1175","volume":"25","author":[{"given":"Katherine","family":"Cocking","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Earth and Environmental Sciences, Cardiff University, Cardiff, United Kingdom"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Michael Bliss","family":"Singer","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Earth and Environmental Sciences, Cardiff University, Cardiff, United Kingdom"},{"name":"Earth Research Institute, University of California, Santa Barbara, Santa Barbara, California"},{"name":"Water Research Institute, Cardiff University, Cardiff, United Kingdom"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"David","family":"MacLeod","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Earth and Environmental Sciences, Cardiff University, Cardiff, United Kingdom"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Mark O.","family":"Cuthbert","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Earth and Environmental Sciences, Cardiff University, Cardiff, United Kingdom"},{"name":"Water Research Institute, Cardiff University, Cardiff, United Kingdom"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Rafael","family":"Rosolem","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"School of Geographical Sciences, University of Bristol, Bristol, England"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Flavian","family":"Muthusi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations, Somalia Water and Land Information Management Project Office, Nairobi, Kenya"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Paolo","family":"Paron","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Food and Agriculture Organization of the United Nations, Somalia Water and Land Information Management Project Office, Nairobi, Kenya"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Joyce","family":"Kimutai","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Kenya Meteorological Department, Nairobi, Kenya"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Phillip","family":"Omondi","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"IGAD Climate Prediction and Application Centre, Nairobi, Kenya"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Ahmed Mohamed","family":"Hassan","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Somali Ministry of Energy and Water Resources, Mogadishu, Somalia"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Asaminew","family":"Teshome","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Ethiopian Meteorological Institute, Addis Ababa, Ethiopia"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Katerina","family":"Michaelides","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Earth Research Institute, University of California, Santa Barbara, Santa Barbara, California"},{"name":"School of Geographical Sciences, University of Bristol, Bristol, England"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"12","reference":[{"key":"bib1","series-title":"J. Climatol. Wea. Forecasting","first-page":"1000204","article-title":"Assessment of drought recurrence in Somaliland: Causes, impacts and mitigations","volume":"5","author":"Abdulkadir, G.","year":"2017","unstructured":"Abdulkadir, G., 2017: \nAssessment of drought recurrence in Somaliland: Causes, impacts and mitigations. J. Climatol. Wea. Forecasting, 5, 1000204, https:\/\/doi.org\/10.4172\/2332-2594.1000204."},{"key":"bib2","author":"Abebe, M.","year":"2006","unstructured":"Abebe, M., 2006: The onset, cessation and dry spells of the small rainy season (Belg) of Ethiopia. 41 pp., https:\/\/ams.confex.com\/ams\/pdfpapers\/136788.pdf."},{"key":"bib3","series-title":"Geophys. Res. Lett.","first-page":"e2022GL099299","article-title":"Sustained water storage in Horn of Africa Drylands dominated by seasonal rainfall extremes","volume":"49","author":"Adloff, M.","year":"2022","unstructured":"Adloff, M., M. B. Singer, D. A. MacLeod, K. Michaelides, N. Mehrnegar, E. Hansford, C. Funk, and D. Mitchell, 2022: \nSustained water storage in Horn of Africa Drylands dominated by seasonal rainfall extremes. Geophys. Res. Lett., 49, e2022GL099299, https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1029\/2022GL099299."},{"key":"bib4","series-title":"J. Hydrometeor.","first-page":"129","article-title":"Validation of satellite rainfall estimates over equatorial East Africa","volume":"23","author":"Ageet, S.","year":"2022","unstructured":"Ageet, S., A. H. Fink, M. Maranan, J. E. Diem, J. Hartter, A. L. Ssali, and P. Ayabagabo, 2022: \nValidation of satellite rainfall estimates over equatorial East Africa. J. Hydrometeor., 23, 129\u2013151, https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1175\/JHM-D-21-0145.1."},{"key":"bib5","series-title":"J. Int. Dev.","first-page":"771","article-title":"Factors influencing pastoral and agropastoral 